## Product

| | |
|--|--|
| Role | Pre-game match-planning coach - not a mid-game consult tool |
| Edition | **11th / #New40k only** |
| Frontend | **GitHub Pages** (simple ask/plan UI) |
| Auth | Firebase Google sign-in; API allowlisted to Dave |
| API | FastAPI on Cloud Run (`europe-west1`), scale-to-zero |
| Data stance | **Consumer only** for rules/facts - never download PDFs, embed, or write the shared corpus. Owns one hand-curated file (`common_builds.yaml`) for likely-opponent-unit notes - not a pipeline. |

Ingest and structured unit publishes live in [roboto-guilliman](https://github.com/Tyberium/roboto-guilliman). Mention that repo only when architecture/data ownership matters - do not frame every task as a Guilliman sibling story.

## Modes (target)

1. **RULES** - cite from shared vector corpus
2. **FACTS** - lookup points / weapons / ability text from structured stores (when published)
3. **COACH** - single tactical question (attachment picks, target priority, "good vs X"); reasons from real profiles/rules; probability claims via the comparative combat-math tool
4. **MATCH PLAN** (flagship) - your list + whatever you know of the opponent, at any input tier; orchestrates COACH across threats, targets, attachments, stratagem budget, deployment, win-conditions into one plan; explicitly flags any guessed opponent units as assumptions

Answer shape: **brief -> why -> rules note -> caveats** for COACH; structured sections for Match Plan.

## North-star

Thousand Sons list in hand, opponent faction known (Tyranids) but no list confirmed: correctly flag the assumed opponent build, get the Rubric-Marine attachment call right by reasoning (not memorized), and back every damage claim with the comparative calculator.

## Hard preferences (until Dave overrides)

- No second ingest/embed pipeline for rules or facts in this repo
- No inventing points, profiles, or hit rates when a lookup misses - say you do not have the data
- **No memorized tactical answers** - attachment picks, target priority, and "good vs" calls must be derived from real profiles/ability text/rules every time, checked against golden evals that score the reasoning process, not stored answers
- Any hit/wound/save/expected-damage claim must go through the comparative (what-if) combat-math tool, never model arithmetic
- **No mid-game live consultation** as a design target - Match Plan is pre-game only
- Auth required from Phase 1 of the API - allowlisted to Dave; unauthenticated requests fail closed
- Photo/vision board-reading is not planned - unreliable without camera calibration
- Opponent-list uncertainty must be stated explicitly, not smoothed over - use tiered inputs (full list / faction+detachment / faction only) and `common_builds.yaml` assumptions, clearly labelled as assumptions
- Standalone first - no Battleplan dependency to ship
- Cheap model for simple asks; stronger model only on COACH/Match Plan when needed

## Phases (see `docs/plan_of_travel.md`)

0. Scaffold (docs) - done
1. Pages + API shell; Firebase Auth allowlist; RULES mode
2. FACTS lookups once corpus publishes units/points
3. Comparative combat-math tool + COACH; golden evals begin (Thousand Sons cases, incl. Rubric attachment)
4. Match Plan (flagship) - tiered inputs, `common_builds.yaml`, full plan orchestration
5. Harden (Pulumi, IAM, rate limits, CI eval gate)

## Persona

Hydra - cunning, multi-angle, meme-aware ("which head is speaking?"). A coach that plans with you before the game, not a wall-of-PDF clerk and not a mid-game crutch.
